## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant secrets strategy, runtime access flow, rotation, and CI safety beyond data isolation.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets Manager per-tenant isolation
- Workload Identity for runtime retrieval
- CMEK-backed encryption and rotation
- CI gate validating cross-tenant access and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
const {SecretManagerServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();
async function accessSecret(tenantId, suffix) {
  const name = `projects/${PROJECT_ID}/secrets/tenant-${tenantId}-${suffix}/versions/latest`;
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({name});
  return version.payload.data.toString('utf8');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rotation impact on live traffic?
- How would you revoke access for a suspended tenant?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design secure, multi-tenant API access patterns using ephemeral tokens, fine-grained IAM controls, and comprehensive security automation. It tests understanding of GCP security primitives, tenant isolation strategies, and operational readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Centralized token issuance with short-lived JWTs
- IAM Conditions for tenant-scoped resource access
- BigQuery Authorized Views for data-level isolation
- API Gateway JWT validation and routing
- Per-tenant CMEK encryption for data protection
- Automated validation and rollback procedures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example IAM policy snippet (illustrative)
{
  "bindings": [
    {
      "role": "roles/bigquery.dataViewer",
      "members": [
        "serviceAccount:tenant-access@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com"
      ],
      "condition": {
        "title": "Tenant Dataset Access",
        "expression": "resource.name.startsWith('projects/project/datasets/tenant-')"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
